        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 24 at 5:48AM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "A Bering Sea low moving through the Bering Strait early Monday\nmorning will move through the Chukchi Sea through the rest of the\nday on Monday. South-southwest winds will increase water levels\nto around 1 to 3 feet above the normal high tide line during the\nMonday and Tuesday high tides from Wainwright to Utqiagvik. Water\nlevels around 2 to 4 feet above the normal high tide line are\npossible from Point Lay to Point Hope. Secondly, winds will shift\nwest-northwest Tuesday afternoon which can prolong high water\nlevels into Wednesday. There is still some uncertainty with the\nexact water level heights and they will be monitored over the next\ncouple of days.",
        "instruction": null,
        "response": "Execute",
