        "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued August 24 at 5:46AM AKDT until August 25 at 4:00PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Water levels of 4 to 6 feet above the normal high tide\nline expected.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern Norton Sound and Nulato Hills.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 PM AKDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Localized beach erosion may occur.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...There remains a relatively small amount of\nuncertainty in forecasted water levels, but confidence has\nincreased. Water levels are expected to peak during the high\ntide Monday morning and then return to normal throughout the\nday. The Tuesday high tide is expected to only be around 1 to 3\nfeet above normal. The highest water levels are expected near\nKoyuk and Elim with Stebbins/St. Michael and Unalakleet near the\nlower end of this range.",
